10	 *
11	 * <p>Points start at 0 and accumulate: {@code +2} when an email address is present,
12	 * {@code +1} when the owner has no namesakes ({@code namesakeCount} is 0), {@code +2}
13	 * for a household of 3 or more, and {@code +3} for a tenure (registration date to today)
14	 * of more than one elapsed fiscal year (the fiscal year starts on 1 July).
15	 *
16	 * <p>Points map to a level: 1 for 0-1 points, 2 for 2-3 points, 3 for 4-5 points, and
17	 * 4 for 6 or more points.
18	 *
19	 * <p>Kept as a standalone helper (rather than a method on {@link OwnerMapper}) so
20	 * MapStruct does not mistake it for a generic mapping method and apply it to unrelated
21	 * fields; the mapper references it only through explicit expressions.
22	 */
